   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nHi Lili,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nIt is great to hear you were able to incorporate your model! I am wondering if you added a plotting function to the plotting directory (see:\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/CCS-Lab/hBayesDM/wiki/Adding-a-new-model-for-a-new-task\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/CCS-Lab/hBayesDM/wiki/Adding-a-new-model-for-a-new-task&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243149808000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3vzyhiXRDBkXW6CIVaLiHl\">\r\nhttps://github.com/CCS-Lab/hBayesDM/wiki/Adding-a-new-model-for-a-new-task</a>)? </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nThis specific file is located here on the github repo: <a href=\"https://github.com/CCS-Lab/hBayesDM/blob/master/R/inst/plotting/plot_functions.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/CCS-Lab/hBayesDM/blob/master/R/inst/plotting/plot_functions.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243149808000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nOV-Yhr73AZ36oxiui26R\">https://github.com/CCS-Lab/hBayesDM/blob/master/R/inst/plotting/plot_functions.R</a></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nIf you add a plotting function with the correct naming scheme there (i.e. &quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(32,31,30);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Web (West European)&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,-apple-system,system-ui,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:15px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline!important\">plot_aversivelearning_delta</span>&quot;)\r\n before running roxygen2::roxygenize(), I think this should fix your problem!</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nBest,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nNate</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hbayesd...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hbayesd...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Lili Zhang &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lili.z...@mail.dcu.ie</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Monday, December 2, 2019 6:23 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> hbayesdm-users &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hbayesd...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> plot function error</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div>"
    ],
