     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>I integrated my own model into the package. Everything works well except for the plot function. I want to plot the posterior distribution of the hyper parameter, but when I run plot(&quot;the hBayesDM object of my model I got&quot;) it shows:</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>Error in plot_aversivelearning_delta(obj = x, fontSize = , ncols = , binSize = ) : </div>\r\n<div>  could not find function &quot;plot_aversivelearning_delta&quot;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Could you think of any causes for this error?</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Thank for your time in advance!</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Best regards,</div>\r\n<div>Lili</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n</div></div>"
